# Bot1 is the monarch. Upkeep of turn 3: both counters go on Ornithopter (2), then doubling makes 4. Upkeep of turn 5: the
# trigger is put on the stack with no targets ("up to two" allows none, an empty Divide), yet the second sentence still
# happens: the four counters already there are doubled to 8. The doubling reads the counters the creature has, not the
# ones this trigger put.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Court of Garenbrig
Ornithopter
Forest x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Court of Garenbrig.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Divide(Ornithopter: 2)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 4
[T5 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Divide()
[T5 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Monarch = Bot1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 8
